msgstr "Stage {0} hat unbekannte Schlüssel: {1}. Gültige Stage-Keys sind: {2}."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Detected a post-aggregation filter alongside `order-by:`, `limit:`, or `fields:` in the same stage. MBQL 5 requires the filter in a separate stage, but those trailing clauses cannot be safely relocated — they may reference pre-aggregation columns that don''t survive the split. Please author this as two stages explicitly: stage 0 with `source-table`, `aggregation`, `breakout`, and any pre-aggregation `filters`; stage 1 with the post-aggregation `filters`, plus `order-by` / `limit` / `fields` that reference the aggregation''s output via cross-stage `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]` refs."
msgstr "Detected a post-aggregation filter alongside `order-by:`, `limit:`, or `fields:` in the same stage. MBQL 5 requires the filter in a separate stage, but those trailing clauses cannot be safely relocated — they may reference pre-aggregation columns that don''t survive the split. Please author this as two stages explicitly: stage 0 with `source-table`, `aggregation`, `Aufschlüsselung`, and any pre-aggregation `filters`; stage 1 with the post-aggregation `filters`, plus `order-by` / `limit` / `fields` that reference the aggregation''s output via cross-stage `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]` refs."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "The query builder''s expression editor rejects a {0} clause in stage {1}: {2}. The query would build but could not be visualized or saved - rewrite the offending clause."
msgstr "Der Expression-Editor des Abfrage-Builder lehnt eine {0}-Klausel in Stage {1} ab: {2}. Die Abfrage würde erstellt werden, konnte aber nicht visualisiert oder gespeichert werden – schreibe die fehlerhafte Klausel um."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Field {0} can be reached from {1} via {2} foreign keys. Specify the `source-field` option on the field clause to disambiguate; call `read_resource` with `metabase://table/<numeric id>/fields` for the source table to list the available foreign-key columns."
msgstr "Feld {0} kann von {1} über {2} Fremdschlüssel erreicht werden. Gib die Option `source-field` in der Feldklausel an, um das zu disambiguieren; rufe `read_resource` mit `metabase://table/<numeric id>/fields` für die Quelltabelle auf, um die verfügbaren Fremdschlüsselspalten aufzulisten."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`field` clause needs a portable FK in its third slot, not a numeric id. Use a vector `[<database>, <schema>, <table>, <column>]` (resolved against the metadata provider) or a string column-name (for cross-stage references)."
msgstr "Die `field`-Klausel benötigt im dritten Slot einen portablen FK, keine numerische ID. Verwende einen Vektor `[<database>, <schema>, <table>, <column>]` (aufgelöst über den Metadata Provider) oder einen String als Spaltennamen (für Cross-Stage-Referenzen)."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Field {0} is on table {1}, which has no foreign key from the source table {2}, so it cannot be reached implicitly. To group or filter by a column from that table, add an explicit `joins:` entry and reference the field using the join alias. If you are aggregating a metric that relates to that table (metrics can join tables that have no foreign key), read that metric dimensions resource `metabase://metric/<metric_id>/dimensions` which lists the exact join clause to paste into `joins:` and the columns it unlocks. Otherwise use a field from the source table."
msgstr "Feld {0} ist in Tabelle {1}, von der es keinen Fremdschlüssel aus der Quelltabelle {2} gibt, daher kann es nicht implizit erreicht werden. Um nach einer Spalte aus dieser Tabelle zu gruppieren oder zu filtern, füge einen expliziten `joins:`-Eintrag hinzu und referenziere das Feld über den Join-Alias. Wenn du eine Metrik aggregierst, die sich auf diese Tabelle bezieht (Metriken können Tabellen joinen, die keinen Fremdschlüssel haben), lies die Ressource für Metrik-Dimensionen `metabase://metric/<metric_id>/dimensions`, die die exakte Join-Klausel zum Einfügen in `joins:` sowie die dadurch freigeschalteten Spalten auflistet. Andernfalls verwende ein Feld aus der Quelltabelle."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`{0}` is not a clause in repr; it was a top-level operation in the older sexp pipeline. {1}"
msgstr "`{0}` ist keine Klausel in repr; es war eine Top-Level-Operation in der älteren sexp-Pipeline. {1}"

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Aggregation index {0} out of range; stage has {1} aggregation(s): {2}"
msgstr "Aggregationsindex {0} außerhalb des gültigen Bereichs; Stage hat {1} Aggregation(en): {2}"

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "No column named {0} is available to reference in this stage. Reference a column by its machine name (e.g. an aggregation is `max`, `count`, `sum` - never its display label like `Max of X`), not a UI label. Available column names: {1}."
msgstr "In dieser Stage ist keine Spalte mit dem Namen {0} verfügbar, auf die verwiesen werden kann. Verweise auf eine Spalte über ihren Machine-Namen (z. B. ist eine Aggregation `max`, `count`, `sum` – niemals ihr Anzeigename wie `Max of X`), nicht über ein UI-Label. Verfügbare Spaltennamen: {1}."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`case` (and `if`) uses its third positional argument as the fallback value, not a `default` key in the options map. Move the value out of the options map and append it as the third arg of the clause: `[case, <opts>, <branch-pairs>, <default>]`. Omit the third arg entirely if you have no fallback (the result will be null on miss)."
msgstr "`case` (und `if`) verwendet sein drittes positionsbasiertes Argument als Fallback-Wert, nicht einen `default`-Key in der Options-Map. Verschiebe den Wert aus der Options-Map und hänge ihn als drittes Arg an die Klausel an: `[case, <opts>, <branch-pairs>, <default>]`. Lass das dritte Arg vollständig weg, wenn du keinen Fallback hast (das Ergebnis ist bei Nichttreffer null)."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Detected a post-aggregation filter (a filter referencing an aggregation from the same stage). MBQL 5 requires this in a separate stage. Auto-fix is unsafe here — either an aggregation''s output column name cannot be derived (e.g. a `metric` reference or unknown head), or two aggregations in this stage would produce the same column name (e.g. two `sum` aggregations on different fields, which lib disambiguates as `sum` / `sum_2` based on field order). Please refactor to multi-stage manually: put the aggregations in stage 0, and the filter in stage 1 referencing the column via a cross-stage `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]` clause. Use an explicit aggregation with a `name` opts override (e.g. `[\"sum\", (opts with key \"name\" → \"sum_total\"), …]`) if you need stable cross-stage names."
msgstr "Detected a post-aggregation filter (a filter referencing an aggregation from the same stage). MBQL 5 requires this in a separate stage. Auto-fix is unsafe here — either an aggregation''s output column name cannot be derived (e.g. a `Metrik` reference or unknown head), or two aggregations in this stage would produce the same column name (e.g. two `sum` aggregations on different fields, which lib disambiguates as `sum` / `sum_2` based on field order). Please refactor to multi-stage manually: put the aggregations in stage 0, and the filter in stage 1 referencing the column via a cross-stage `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]` clause. Use an explicit aggregation with a `name` opts override (e.g. `[\"sum\", (opts with key \"name\" → \"sum_total\"), …]`) if you need stable cross-stage names."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Field {0} is reachable from {1} explicit joins via aliases {2}. Specify the `source-field-join-alias` option on the field clause to pick which join''s foreign key to use."
msgstr "Feld {0} ist über {1} explizite Joins über Aliase {2} erreichbar. Gib die Option `source-field-join-alias` in der Field-Klausel an, um auszuwählen, welchen Fremdschlüssel des Joins verwendet werden soll."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`[expression, <opts>, <name>]` reference requires a non-blank string identifier in the third slot, matching an entry in some stage''s `expressions:` block."
msgstr "Eine Referenz vom Typ `[expression, <opts>, <name>]` erfordert im dritten Slot einen nicht-leeren String-Identifier, der zu einem Eintrag in einem Stage-`expressions:`-Block passt."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Found an integer-indexed aggregation reference but this stage has no `aggregation:` clause"
msgstr "Eine integer-indexierte Aggregationsreferenz gefunden, aber diese Stage hat keine `aggregation:`-Klausel"

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Stage {0} aggregation entry {1} is a `field` clause, not an aggregation. The `aggregation:` block expects aggregation functions like `count`, `sum`, `avg`, `metric`, etc. - or wrap the field in one (e.g. `[sum, <opts>, <field>]`). If you wanted to group by this column, use `breakout:` instead."
msgstr "Stage {0} Aggregationseintrag {1} ist eine `field`-Klausel, keine Aggregation. Der `aggregation:`-Block erwartet Aggregationsfunktionen wie `count`, `sum`, `avg`, `metrik` usw. – oder wickle das Feld in eine solche ein (z. B. `[sum, <opts>, <field>]`). Wenn du nach dieser Spalte Gruppieren nach wolltest, verwende stattdessen `Aufschlüsselung:`."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/resolve.clj
msgid "Invalid temporal literal {0} in :absolute-datetime — use an ISO-8601 date, datetime, year, or year-month."
msgstr "Ungültiges temporales Literal {0} in :absolute-datetime — verwende ein ISO-8601-Datum, datetime, Jahr oder Jahr-Monat."

#: metabase/ai_tracing/api.clj
msgid "Eval trace not found"
msgstr "Eval-Trace nicht gefunden"

#: metabase/ai_tracing/settings.clj
msgid "Enable eval-time AI agent trace capture. When true, agent / MCP / agent-api runs capture a full trace (prompts, completions, tool I/O, custom spans) and write it as structured JSONL to a per-session file via the dedicated `metabase.ai-tracing.log` logger. Separate from MB_TRACING_ENABLED. Off by default; intended for dedicated eval instances, NOT production (traces contain full, unredacted user content)."
msgstr "Aktiviere das Eval-Time-Trace-Capturing für KI-Agenten. Wenn true, erfassen Agent-/MCP-/agent-api-Ausführungen einen vollständigen Trace (Prompts, Completions, Tool-I/O, benutzerdefinierte Spans) und schreiben ihn als strukturiertes JSONL über den dedizierten Logger `metabase.ai-tracing.log` in eine sitzungsspezifische Datei. Getrennt von MB_TRACING_ENABLED. Standardmäßig aus; gedacht für dedizierte Eval-Instanzen, NICHT für die Produktion (Traces enthalten vollständige, unredigierte Benutzerinhalte)."

